    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d231">

                <pb facs="0293" n="223" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg223"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/2621: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morgan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-19T17:00:00-05:00"
                            >November 19, 1918—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your November 15, 1 p.m. Department feels that it is not essential for Brazil to
                    be represented at the preliminary conferences. Please say to Da Gama that Department considers it desirable
                    that he should go to the peace conference and wishes to advise him for his very
                    confidential information that it understands that the peace conference will
                    probably meet in the middle of the month of January next.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
